\section{The signal}

This note reports a transit candidate on \VAR{n.name}\BLOCK{if n.gaia_id} (Gaia DR3 \VAR{n.gaia_id}\BLOCK{if n.gmag}, $G = \VAR{n.gmag}$\BLOCK{endif})\BLOCK{endif}, a star that Kepler recorded only in the background of other targets' pixels. A dip of \VAR{n.depth} ppm lasting \VAR{n.duration} hours repeats every \VAR{n.period} days in its KBonus Kepler Background light curve \citep{kbonus}, with the first mid-transit at BJD$_{\rm TDB}$ \VAR{n.t0_bjd} (BKJD \VAR{n.t0_bkjd}). It remains a candidate until independent follow-up confirms it.

